# The other half of the same command. A patch that deletes a key carries the
# whole key in its text, so the bytes cross exactly as an added one's do -- and
# a modification hunk emits both markers at once, from one `git diff`.
#
# `-` is not in the base64 alphabet, so no layout reached this one by accident.
# The plain form is here rather than the encrypted one because the encrypted
# layout is already carried by the added fixture beside it, and what this file
# is for is the marker.
#
# Its header line opens with six dashes: the marker lands on the header's own
# leading five, and the capture starts at the second.
#
# Produced by `git diff --cached`, not written by hand: git 2.55.0, 2026-09-19.

diff --git a/deploy/tls.key b/deploy/tls.key
deleted file mode 100644
index 597d288..0000000
--- a/deploy/tls.key
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,4 +0,0 @@
------BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
-QUJDREVGR0hJSktMTU5PUFFSU1RVVldYWVowMTIzNDU2Nzg5YWJjZGVmZ2hpamts
-bW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXpBQkNERUZHSElKS0xNTk9QUVJTVFVWV1hZWjAxMjM0NTY3
------END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
